<Base><div class="container"><div class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Applied Data Scientist · PhD in Sport Performance Analysis</div><h1>Finding insights where conventional metrics fall short.</h1><p class="lead">I turn complex data into meaningful events, predictive models, and decision-relevant insights — combining statistical rigor, original algorithms, and real-world domain understanding.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#work">Explore my work ↓</a><a class="btn alt" href="https://github.com/supolabence">View GitHub ↗</a></div></div><section id="work"><div class="eyebrow">Selected work</div><h2>Research turned into applied data science</h2><p class="section-intro">Three peer-reviewed studies, presented as practical case studies: the problem, the analytical solution, the evaluation, and the transferable engineering skills.</p><div class="cards">{projects.map(p=><article class="card"><div class="card-img"><img src={p.img} alt={`Unpublished analysis visualization illustrating ${p.title}`} loading="lazy"/></div><div class="card-content"><span class="tag">{p.tag}</span><h3 style="margin-top:10px">{p.title}</h3><p>{p.desc}</p><a href={p.url}>Explore case study →</a></div></article>)}</div></section><section id="about"><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h2>Research mindset. Practical execution.</h2><p class="section-intro">I hold a PhD in Sport Performance Analysis from the University of Vienna and bring over seven years of experience at IBM, including work in data science. My research combines spatio-temporal data, feature engineering, statistical modeling and interpretable machine learning. I also work directly with athletes and teams through my coaching practice, Flowletes.</p><div class="skills">{['Python','Pandas','NumPy','Statistical Modeling','Machine Learning','Feature Engineering','Model Evaluation','Spatial Analytics'].map(s=><span class="skill">{s}</span>)}</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;margin-top:16px">Research projects were collaborative publications; my individual contribution included their programming and technical implementation.</p></div></section><section id="publications"><div class="eyebrow">Publications</div><h2>Peer-reviewed research</h2><div class="prose"><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0281467">Modeling the formation of defensive gaps in basketball: Cutting on a teammate’s drive</a> (2023)</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.2478/IJCSS-2023-0002">Modeling the extra pass in basketball – an assessment of one of the most crucial skills for creating great ball movement</a> (2023)</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/24748668.2022.2039090">The role of secondary assists in basketball: An analysis of its characteristics and effect on scoring</a> (2022)</p></div></section><section><div class="next"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#a7ebe0">What comes next</div><h2>From published research to interactive applications</h2><p>A future applied project will explore game momentum and coaching decisions using event-level basketball data. The portfolio is designed to grow as new projects are completed.</p></div></section></div></Base>
